# Ρ·telemetry·share — the TRACKED template for the gitignored .githooks/local.env.
#
# The endpoints are per-clone POINTERS (each machine sets its own), which is the right shape and
# is why local.env is gitignored.  What was missing is that the shape was invisible: a fresh clone
# had no way to learn these knobs exist, and an EXISTING clone had no way to learn its values had
# gone stale.  Measured cost — VM/VLogs migrated to k8s NodePorts on 2026-08-26, this clone kept
# pushing at the retired ports for a day, and every run's telemetry was lost SILENTLY because the
# pushers are best-effort by design: a `Connection refused` cannot fail a commit and so said
# nothing.  ⚑ A POINTER THAT GOES STALE SILENTLY IS THE DEFECT, NOT THE POINTER.
#
# Copy to .githooks/local.env and uncomment what this machine actually runs.  Absent ⇒ silent
# no-op, which stays correct: telemetry that can fail a commit is a liability, not an instrument.
# The values below are THIS machine's as of 2026-08-27 and are an example, never an authority —
# ports move, and the hook now probes each one and says so rather than failing quietly.
# ⚑ PORTS MOVED 2026-08-26: VM/VLogs migrated from host quadlets to k8s pods and now answer on
# LOOPBACK-PINNED NodePorts (30828/30928).  The old 8428/9428 are retired and REFUSE — measured,
# both closed.  We pushed at them for a day and lost every run's telemetry, silently, because the
# pushers are best-effort by design: a `Connection refused` cannot fail a commit and so said
# nothing.  ⚑ A POINTER THAT GOES STALE SILENTLY IS THE DEFECT, NOT THE POINTER — the env-var
# indirection is right and held a dead value.  BES (:1985) did NOT move; verified open.
# Ρ·telemetry: push build-loop timing to cassian-observability's OTLP store (host-loopback VM,
# host-netns direct — otlp_push runs in the pre-commit shell, outside any bazel sandbox).
# export PAPERKIT_OTLP_METRICS=http://127.0.0.1:30828/opentelemetry/v1/metrics

# Ρ·telemetry·logs — the FINDINGS sink (VictoriaLogs).  Distinct from the metrics endpoint above:
# that one carries build-loop TIMING and only on a green hook; this one carries the RESIDUAL a red
# gate computed, and fires on red especially.  Happy-path-only telemetry loses exactly the runs
# worth keeping.
# export PAPERKIT_LOGS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:30928/insert/jsonline

# Ρ·telemetry·bes — Bazel's own Build Event Stream to the local BuildBuddy.  Structurally better
# than parsing a log: BES is Bazel's FIRST-PARTY event protocol (per-target results, per-action
# timing, the invocation's own id), so it cannot drift from a text format the engine may reword.
# The log parser stays for what BES does not carry — the ENGINE's residual (a coherence GROUNDING
# line lives in an action's stderr, not in a build event).
# export PAPERKIT_BES=grpc://127.0.0.1:1985
